2. MANAGEMENT & COMPUTE CLI TROUBLESHOOTING ACTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OVS Bridge Creation    sudo ovs-vsctl add-br br-compute                Manually force-create a secondary OVS bridge via CLI
OVS Bridge Creation    sudo ovs-vsctl add-bond br-compute bond-c ens3f0 ens3f1  Directly provision an OVS-managed trunk bond
OVS Bridge Creation    sudo ovs-vsctl del-br br-compute                Destroy an obsolete or misconfigured OVS bridge

OVS Port Profiling     sudo ovs-vsctl show                             Verify full virtual switch map and active bonds
OVS Port Profiling     sudo ovs-vsctl list-ports br-compute            List all physical/virtual ports bound to compute
OVS Port Profiling     sudo ovs-vsctl port-to-br <port_name>           Identify which bridge a specific interface belongs to
OVS Port Profiling     sudo ovs-ofctl dump-flows br-compute            Dump low-level OpenFlow rules driving the switch data

KVM Net Management     sudo virsh net-list --all                       Verify status of all CLI-defined guest networks
KVM Net Management     sudo virsh net-destroy <net_name>               Forcefully stop/deactivate a virtual network domain
KVM Net Management     sudo virsh net-undefine <net_name>              Completely delete a network domain definition
KVM Net Management     sudo virsh net-edit <net_name>                  Open active network XML config file in default editor

Fabric Verification    sudo ovs-appctl bond/show bond-compute          Check physical LACP/Bond hashing and link alignments
Fabric Verification    sudo ip link set dev br-compute up              Force state of compute bridge to UP at kernel level
Fabric Verification    sudo tcpdump -i br-compute -n -e vlan 100       Sniff traffic specifically tagged on VLAN 100
Fabric Verification    sudo ip route show table all                    Print comprehensive system routing profiles
